  "2026-10-23T08:25:45.901Z",codex-agent,"Ownership check: this repository only configures the reusable pm-github closeout workflow and package version. Delivery candidate selection and chronology are implemented in pm-github closeout.ts (runCloseout), not in pm-ado configuration. Issue #33 belongs to pm-github selection/provenance logic; no existing history rewritten and no item closed here."
  "2026-11-06T15:12:39.809Z",codex-sol,"Read issue 33 and its full discussion. Main 0b3d5a3 already contains the record correction from merged PR 44 (9f7158b): PR 19 is the delivery, completed_at is its merge time, and history appends the correction without rewriting earlier records. PR 32 is closed. Reproduce the original static comparison and verify PR 19 checks before preparing an evidence-only closeout; no production code change is warranted. The original matcher lives outside this repository and will not be modified."
  "2026-11-06T15:14:07.398Z",codex-sol,"Static reproduction verified through PmClient in two real non-git temp trackers, loading immutable item/history bytes without SDK mocks: reported PR 32 head 1b1ab501 selects PR 16 and completed_at 2026-10-04T12:58:08.000Z; origin/main selects PR 19 and completed_at 2026-10-08T01:19:51.000Z. Current actual_result and close_reason include PR 19, its merge SHA f297a71431debfe2e00adb8dd1b02874e6dadfe2 and merge time; resolution explicitly rejects PR 16 as delivery. The close event cites PR 19, the following correction records its completion date, all four implementation comments remain, and pre-PR-44 history is a byte-identical prefix. No changes to the already-correct closed item are needed. GitHub verifies PR 19 head 119b225ec6f84bf8c53ee6c953dba0980ddc6f1a: Node 22, Node 26, codeql and CodeQL SUCCESS; skipped/neutral reviewer checks are not review approval. PR 44 merged at 2026-10-24T23:23:14Z. This acceptance concerns static provenance and offline enforcement, not live Azure."
  "2026-11-06T15:17:53.885Z",codex-sol,"Identical delivery assertions reject the original PR 32 snapshot with an AssertionError and pass current main, in disposable non-git trackers read through PmClient. This is a historical-data sensitivity check; no new implementation or source-function revert is applicable because PR 44 already corrected this repository. The owner discussion identifies the matcher and its class regression as pm-github-owned; that separate implementation is not independently re-reviewed here. Existing linked enforcement tests PASS 3/3, zero skipped; pm test also PASS 3/3 with result tracking disabled by policy. Strict health reports pre-existing extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew (CLI 2026.11.4 versus managed host 2026.11.5), independently reproduced against unchanged main; follow-up pm-ado-extension-host-skew tracks it. No dependency pin or threshold change is part of this closeout."
  "2026-11-06T15:18:31.904Z",codex-sol,"Preparing an evidence-only closeout PR: production source and existing pm-ado-5w3m item/history remain unchanged. Typecheck and focused tests pass; the docstring gate and test compilation are being verified. No lint script is declared. Full npm release:check has been invoked at unchanged thresholds; remote CI will run the complete Node 22/26 and npm/Bun release gates on the pushed head. Final run results and bot-review rounds will be reported on the PR. The issue item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification, with this agent claim released. Tracked scope is this issue item/history, the discovered health follow-up item/history, and the generated changelog."
  "2026-11-06T19:12:02.171Z",codex-sol,"Resumed PR 91 at cfd70d8 after the orchestrator reported two CodeRabbit findings. Prior exact-head Node 22/26, npm/Bun release gates and CodeQL passed; do not rerun that finished work. The review correctly observes that statement-gate tests do not guard delivery provenance. Add a permanent SDK/non-git tracker regression for the existing PR 19 record and append-only completion evidence, plus an isolated real-generator fixture that checks Unreleased content after a release tag. Keep production logic, thresholds and the already-correct delivery item/history unchanged. Document mutation sensitivity in disposable fixture copies and link the new repeatable commands before pushing."
  "2026-11-06T19:20:26.802Z",codex-sol,"Both CodeRabbit findings are addressed by repeatable tests. test/closeout-provenance.test.ts reads the shipped delivery item and validated native history through the pinned SDK in a real non-git temp tracker; it pins PR 19, merge f297a71431debfe2e00adb8dd1b02874e6dadfe2 and merge time 2026-10-08T01:19:51Z, and checks record/history/close evidence consistency. test/release-workflow.test.ts now executes the actual changelog:full script against a real SDK tracker and synthetic release tag, asserting generated Unreleased content retains the pending item and the existing release. Child Git context and credential variables are excluded; fixture commits use the required public bot identity. No production code, coverage thresholds, dependency pins or existing delivery history changed."
  "2026-11-06T19:20:32.966Z",codex-sol,"Mutation proofs in disposable copies only: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/closeout-provenance.test.ts passes 1/1 with current record/history, fails 0/1 with AssertionError after restoring the original PR 32 snapshot selecting PR 16, also fails 0/1 when only its historical stream is restored, then passes 1/1 after restoring current bytes. node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern='changelog:full retains' test/release-workflow.test.ts passes 1/1; disabling only the copied generator release-window branch for Unreleased makes it fail 0/1 at the missing-section assertion; restoring that function passes 1/1. The actual package dependencies and historical records were never mutated."
  "2026-11-06T19:20:40.882Z",codex-sol,"Validation after the review changes: node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/closeout-provenance.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts PASS 13/13, zero failures/skips; the linked pinned pm test --run --only-last --progress also PASS 13/13, and isolated Git-config rerun PASS 13/13. npm run build:test, npm run typecheck, npm run docstring and git diff --check PASS; docstrings remain 128 declarations in 19 files, and there is no lint script. Native history patch types are derived from the SDK rather than weakened. Fresh exact-head CI and CodeRabbit round 2 will be requested on https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/91; prior green CI at cfd70d8 is historical evidence only. Releasing the claim without closing the item; the changelog will be regenerated after this final tracker write."
  "2026-11-06T19:33:42.986Z",codex-sol,"Pre-CI integration inspection caught an overbroad environment filter in the new changelog fixture: removing every PM_ key also removes PM_ADO_STATEMENT_SOURCES and PM_ADO_STATEMENT_REPORT_DIR while retaining NODE_OPTIONS, which would break the inherited statement preloader. Narrowed the filter to inherited Git context and credential/npm configuration keys, preserving coverage settings. This affects only the new fixture. Running its real CLI through both coverage passes in a disposable sentinel project at unchanged 100% thresholds before the corrective push; do not use the intermediate 3e7b112 head as final evidence."
  "2026-11-06T19:36:22.690Z",codex-sol,"Coverage integration proof completed: the real release-workflow suite passes both V8 and statement-preloader execution in a disposable sentinel project with all four thresholds at 100% (1/1 independent statements). Restoring only the broad PM_ environment filter in a disposable test copy lets the V8 pass succeed but makes the statement-preloaded CLI fail with ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE; restoring the narrow filter makes both passes pass again. npm run build:test also passes. This sentinel probe establishes subprocess instrumentation compatibility, not the package-wide coverage claim; fresh final-head CI must still measure the unchanged configured source scope. Prior review replies remain valid, both threads are resolved, and the corrective commit will be pushed with these pm records before re-queueing review."
  "2026-11-06T19:40:43.781Z",codex-sol,"CodeQL opened an additional thread on the provenance test URL substring assertion (PRRT_kwDOUMUq1860qUCI). This is test code rather than a runtime URL sanitizer, but an exact comparison is the stronger contract: compare the entire structured delivery receipt prefix against the exact PR 19 URL, merge revision and merge time instead of accepting separate substrings. The package's production behavior remains unchanged. Re-run the focused native tracker test and prove a coherent fixture containing a foreign URL with the expected URL embedded is rejected before the next push."
  "2026-11-06T19:43:08.981Z",codex-sol,"CodeQL thread PRRT_kwDOUMUq1860qUCI is addressed by exact structured receipt comparison in test/closeout-provenance.test.ts. The current native tracker test passes 1/1 and npm run build:test passes. A disposable real tracker was initialized through the SDK, seeded with the original item/history, then updated through PmClient.update so actual_result contained a foreign URL embedding the expected PR 19 URL. The valid native audit stream and matching materialized update are rejected specifically by the exact-receipt assertion (expected FAIL 0/1); restoring the original fixture bytes passes 1/1. This improves the test oracle without introducing runtime URL validation or changing production behavior. Both original CodeRabbit threads remain fixed and resolved; the CodeQL thread will be answered after this push. Fresh final-head CI/review must verify the correction; previous heads are not final evidence."
  "2026-11-07T23:50:19.457Z",codex-agent,"PR 91 review round: fetched all review threads and comments (no pagination remains), plus the latest CodeRabbit review. One unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOUMUq1860t9tF is valid: latest-write assertions alone do not preserve the pre-PR-44 event prefix. Pin its bytes to a SHA-256 reference independently obtained from immutable commit 42170123973a632f51fbcbb128823583c9315c5a; retain current SDK, record and close-receipt assertions. Merge of origin/main completed first without conflicts. The latest review has no Outside diff range section. Its scope warning concerns the changelog fixture requested by resolved thread PRRT_kwDOUMUq1860n-RH and already linked here for active issue 33, so retaining that regression is justified. Review the whole PR for equivalent provenance gaps and prove historical mutation sensitivity in disposable copies only."
  "2026-11-07T23:53:07.019Z",codex-agent,"Regression and behavioral revert proof for PRRT_kwDOUMUq1860t9tF: immutable pre-PR-44 commit 42170123973a632f51fbcbb128823583c9315c5a contains 17 history events, 27087 bytes, SHA-256 1c004298e4879ab71a2447b6e5a4c57b174a66a9df6bc1768707820a8c99621a, and is still a byte-identical prefix. Added raw prefix-length/digest assertions while preserving all SDK, record, latest-write and close-receipt checks. In a disposable non-git package copy, node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/closeout-provenance.test.ts passes 1/1 on original history; editing only the first event message and recomputing its valid SDK record hash fails 0/1 specifically on the prefix assertion; reverting only the added check makes the identical historical mutation pass 1/1; restoring the check fails 0/1 again; restoring original history passes 1/1. Tracked history was never changed. Whole-PR review found no additional instance of this defect class: exact delivery receipt checks and real generated Unreleased-content checks remain intact. Linked pm test --run --progress passes both commands (3/3 statement tests plus 13/13 provenance/release tests, zero skips); identity/privacy audit passes 4/4. Build, build:test, typecheck and docstring pass (128 declarations in 19 files). No lint script exists. Begin bounded serial npm and Bun full release gates with unchanged thresholds; recent CI gates took about 20 minutes apiece, so limit their combined local run to 55 minutes and defer any unfinished full gate to CI."
  "2026-11-08T01:24:41.231Z",codex-agent,"Resumed PR 91 review round after an interrupted local run. Remote branch fetched and pulled with fast-forward-only; the existing local merge already contains current origin/main. Preserving the existing uncommitted provenance guard and append-only tracker records, then independently rechecking its immutable reference, disposable behavioral revert proof and final gates. Latest remote review inventory still has exactly one unresolved thread and no Outside diff range findings. No review replies or resolutions will be posted."
  "2026-11-08T01:26:42.764Z",codex-agent,"Independent resumed verification: pre-PR-44 reference commit 42170123973a632f51fbcbb128823583c9315c5a has exactly 17 events and 27087 bytes; its SHA-256 matches the new guard. A disposable non-git package copy passes 1/1, then changing only the first event message and resealing it with the pinned SDK produces a valid audit stream with every later event unchanged. Fixed test rejects it 0/1 at the immutable-prefix assertion; removing only the new prefix check makes the same mutation pass 1/1; restoring the check rejects it 0/1; restoring original history passes 1/1. Real history is untouched. Linked pm tests pass 3/3 statement cases and 13/13 provenance/release cases, zero skips. Typecheck, build, build:test, docstring (128 declarations in 19 files), identity/privacy audit (4/4), unchanged committed dist and base-history prefix checks pass. No lint script exists. Strict health retains only the separately tracked extension host version skew as a failure. Starting serial npm and Bun release checks in isolated Git/HOME contexts with a combined 55-minute cap, two test workers and unchanged thresholds."
  "2026-11-08T01:46:25.750Z",codex-agent,"Final local gate decision for PR 91: npm run release:check reached its first V8 suite after passing typecheck, build and docstring, but that first pass alone was still running after about 19 minutes. Because the release gate repeats the suite for independent statement coverage and Bun repeats the full gate, the combined npm/Bun runtime now projects beyond the approximately 60-minute local budget. Ended the local attempt deliberately after 1124 seconds and deferred both complete release checks to fresh CI at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/91/checks. The resulting interrupted sync test-file receipt is cancellation evidence, not a completed failing gate; there is no complete local coverage result. Bun full gate was not started. No assertion failure was reported before deliberate termination. Separate npm run test:native-precondition passes exactly 19/19 with zero skips, npm run verify:release-publish-attestation validates the publish invocation, and npm run verify:release-changelog-date validates all four generator invocations and its behavioral date probe. Linked tests remain 3/3 plus 13/13; identity/privacy is 4/4; typecheck, build, build:test, docstring and unchanged dist pass. Full npm/Bun certification remains pending CI; strict local health retains the existing extension-host skew tracked separately. Whole-PR self-review found no additional provenance defect. The latest review has no Outside diff range findings; its scope warning is declined because the generated-Unreleased regression was explicitly requested in resolved thread PRRT_kwDOUMUq1860n-RH and is linked to this active issue. Releasing only this agent claim, leaving the item in progress. Regenerate the changelog after the release write, then verify all changed history streams remain prefix extensions of main, audit the final commit identity, and push without replying to or resolving any review thread."
